  <model metaid="meta_dapagliflozin_intestine" id="dapagliflozin_intestine" name="Model for dapagliflozin absorption in the small intestine" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for dapagliflozin absorption</h1>
        <ul>
          <li>Dissolution of the oral dose and absorption of dapagliflozin; the
fraction absorbed <code>F_dap_abs</code> of the dapagliflozin of the lumen is
absorbed, the rest is excreted in the feces. After an oral solution of
50 mg of 14C-dapagliflozin 21 % of the radioactivity is recovered in the
feces, 15.4 % of the dose as unchanged dapagliflozin [Obermeier2010];
the absolute bioavailability is 78 % [Boulton2013].</li>
          <li>The enterohepatic circulation is minimal and not modeled.</li>
          <li>Food (<code>fed</code>) slows the absorption (<code>FED_f_absorption</code>): a high fat meal
lowers Cmax by 31 % and delays tmax by about 1 hr, the AUC is unchanged
[Kasichayanula2011b].</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
